      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "GrabCut foreground extraction\n\n'CV Annotate Points' is the interaction: RUN ONCE to load the photo into the node, then LEFT-CLICK around the object (drag to fine-tune, SHIFT+CLICK to remove). The same clicks seed GrabCut two ways:\n\n- RECTANGLE INIT (top): the points' bounding box goes into the 'points' input - everything outside the box is sure background, the inside is refined from color statistics. 2 points (opposite corners) are enough.\n- POLYGON INIT (bottom): the annotate node's polygon mask goes into the 'mask' input as PROBABLE FOREGROUND - with 3+ points hugging the silhouette this seeds tighter than a box and survives objects that touch the frame.\n\nEach branch previews the cutout (cv2.bitwise_and through the foreground mask), the raw 4-value GrabCut label map as a heatmap (sure/probable x fg/bg - watch the probable ring shrink onto the object), and inspects 'success'. Failure tolerance: too few points (or a box covering the whole frame) gives success=false and an empty mask instead of an error."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
